      "text": "The vector on the line is given by the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{v_0} + t\\mathbf{v_{\\parallel}},$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{v_0}$ is the initial vector, and $\\mathbf{v_{\\parallel}}$ is a parallel vector.\n\nBy using the vector equation of a line, we get\n\n$$\\mathbf{v}_0 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} v_{x0} \\\\ v_{y0} \\end{pmatrix},$$\n\nand\n\n$$\\mathbf{v_{\\parallel}} = \\begin{pmatrix} v_{x_1 - x_0} \\\\ v_{y_1 - y_0} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 8 \\end{pmatrix}$$\n\n(Notice a key piece of information: the vector at $t = 2$ has $\\mathbf{v_{\\parallel}} ($after scaling) as $\\begin{pmatrix} v_{x_1 - x_0} \\mathbf{a} \\\\ v_{y_1 - y_0} \\mathbf{a} \\end{pmatrix},$ which is just a scaling of $\\begin{pmatrix} v_{x0} \\\\ v_{y0} \\end{pmatrix}:$ if we swap $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix},$ then we get $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 8 \\end{pmatrix}.$ ), where $\\mathbf{a}$ is a constant that needs to be determined.\n\nPlugging into the vector equation of the line, we get\n\n$$v_{x_0} + 2t v_{a} = 1$$\n\nand\n\n$$v_{y_0} + 8t v_{a} = 4.$$\n\nSolving for $v_{ay},$ we get\n\n$$v_{ay} = \\frac{v_{y0} + v_{x_0}}{2t} = \\frac{-3 + 1}{8} = -\\frac{1}{4}.$$\n\nFrom the above equation of the line,\n\n$$\\mathbf{v}_{x}(\\mathbf{t} = -7) = v_{x_0} + t v_{a} = 1 + 2(-7) = -13,$$\n$$\\mathbf{v}_{y}(\\mathbf{t} = -7) = v_{y_0} + 8t v_{a} = 4 + 8(-7)(-\\frac{1}{4}) = 3.$$\n\nSo the vector on the line at $t = -7$ is $\\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}.$\n\nAns: $\\boxed{(-13, 3)}$.\n\nThis problem is a three-dimensional translation of Two-Dimensional Translation problem. Switching around the scaling vector appropriately provides a quaint 2-dimensional translation.",
